From d081de2146cbfecb546ea876d664c0c1706156e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:35:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 078/137] media: qcom: camss: Keep the SM8350 PHY timer at 300
 MHz up to 2.5 Gb/s

The CSIPHY wants its timer clock above a quarter of the link frequency,
which at the wide camera's 1248 MHz (2496 Mb/s per lane) is more than the
SM8350 timer's 300 MHz. The vendor driver runs the timer at 300 MHz at
every rate, and the IMX563 streams at 2496 Mb/s with it without receiver
errors: on SM8350 use the highest level instead of failing.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
index 539ac4888b60..92816f1d2e5a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -162,6 +162,14 @@ static int csiphy_set_clock_rates(struct csiphy_device *csiphy)
 				if (min_rate < clock->freq[j])
 					break;
 
+			/*
+			 * SM8350: the vendor driver runs the PHY timer at
+			 * 300 MHz for every rate, 2.5 Gb/s per lane included.
+			 */
+			if (j == clock->nfreqs &&
+			    csiphy->camss->res->version == CAMSS_8350)
+				j = clock->nfreqs - 1;
+
 			if (j == clock->nfreqs) {
 				dev_err(dev,
 					"Pixel clock is too high for CSIPHY\n");
